  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best config (config_033, acc=0.7250) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile. scgpt was clearly inferior (0.520), and scvi_n200 consistently outperforms across tested settings. However, pca_n2000 has never been tested in the optimal multimodal configuration space. This experiment (config_011: pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted + multiprofile) is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder, isolating whether the learned scvi representation is truly necessary or whether a simpler linear PCA projection suffices. If pca_n2000 is competitive, it confirms the bottleneck is elsewhere and frees future experiments to explore other dimensions; if it is substantially worse, it firmly validates scvi_n200 and lets us focus the remaining 3 experiments on confirming the best config's robustness or testing marginal variants. With only 3 experiments left after this one, reducing uncertainty on the most impactful untested variable (RNA encoder) in the top-performing configuration is the highest-value use of this slot."
}

